L-inflation | Front page | | pressing.variable == 'inflation' | figures.inflation;figures.inflation_change | shocks;figures.inflation_before | CH-inflation | reporter | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write the lead on inflation: where it stands against the target, which way it moved since the quarter before, and what this quarter's new shocks have to do with it.
L-jobs | Front page | | pressing.variable == 'unemployment' | figures.unemployment;figures.unemployed_persons | drivers.output | CH-unemployment | reporter | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write the lead on unemployment: how many people are out of work, how far unemployment stands from its natural rate, and why.
L-growth | Front page | | pressing.variable == 'growth' | figures.growth | shocks | CH-output | reporter | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write the lead on growth: how fast output grew against its trend, and what this quarter's new shocks have to do with it.
L-wages | Front page | | pressing.variable == 'wages' | figures.wage_inflation;figures.inflation;figures.wage_real | | CH-wages | reporter | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write the lead on wages: how fast they rise, and how that compares with prices.
L-calm | Front page | | TRUE | figures.inflation;figures.growth;figures.unemployment | | CH-inflation | reporter | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write the lead on a calm quarter: inflation, growth and unemployment all stand close to their normal levels. Say so plainly, and tell readers what such a quarter means for them.
E-cause | The Economy | | figures.output_fell | figures.growth;drivers.output | figures.unemployment | CH-output | reporter;business;economist | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about why output fell last quarter: how much it shrank and what moved it most.
E-demand | The Economy | | shock('demand') | shocks.demand | figures.growth | CH-output | reporter;business;household | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about this quarter's change in how much households and firms want to spend: which way it goes and how strong it is.
E-productivity | The Economy | | shock('technology') | shocks.technology | figures.growth;figures.inflation | CH-output | business;economist | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about this quarter's change in how much firms can produce with the same work, and what it means for firms.
E-growth | The Economy | | TRUE | figures.growth | | CH-output | reporter | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | Write a short report on how fast the economy grew last quarter, measured against its trend.
P-costs | Prices and Wages | | shock('costs') | shocks.costs;figures.inflation | figures.wage_inflation | CH-inflation | reporter;household;economist | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about this quarter's change in firms' costs, and how it passes on to the prices people pay.
P-inflation | Prices and Wages | | abs(figures.inflation - law.target) > threshold('inflation') | figures.inflation | public.expected_inflation;figures.inflation_change | CH-inflation | reporter;critic;household | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about inflation standing away from the target: how far, which way, and how people feel it.
P-wages | Prices and Wages | | abs(figures.wage_inflation - law.wage_normal) > threshold('wages') | figures.wage_inflation;figures.inflation;figures.wage_real | figures.unemployment | CH-wages | household;business;economist | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about wages rising faster or more slowly than their normal pace, and how that compares with prices.
P-steady | Prices and Wages | | TRUE | figures.inflation | figures.wage_inflation | CH-inflation | reporter | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | Write a short report on how fast prices rose last quarter.
J-slump | Jobs | | figures.quarters_above_natural >= 4 | figures.unemployment;figures.unemployed_persons;figures.quarters_above_natural | | CH-unemployment | household;critic;reporter | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about unemployment that has stayed above its natural rate for many quarters: how many people are out of work, and for how long the job market has been weak.
J-count | Jobs | | TRUE | figures.unemployment;figures.unemployed_persons | | CH-unemployment | reporter | FALSE | TRUE | TRUE | Write a short report on the job market: the unemployment rate and how many people are out of work.
M-word | Markets and the Bank | word | word.judged | word.announced;word.kept | public.trust_percent;word.room | CH-rate | markets;critic;economist | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about whether the central bank kept its word this quarter: the policy rate it had announced, the rate it set, and whether the announcement counts as kept or broken.
M-liftoff | Markets and the Bank | | public.spell > 0 | public.spell | figures.rate;shocks.path_length;word.path | CH-rate | markets;economist | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about how long the public expects the policy rate to stay at zero.
M-aim | Markets and the Bank | aim | abs(public.aim_change) >= threshold('m_aim') | public.perceived_aim;public.aim_change | public.expected_inflation | CH-expectations | critic;markets;economist | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about the public's changing view of the inflation rate the central bank is really aiming at.
M-decision | Markets and the Bank | | TRUE | figures.rate | public.expected_inflation;public.trust_percent | CH-rate | reporter;markets | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | Write a short report on the central bank's last decision on the policy rate.
G-result | Politics | politics | government.vote_held | government.vote_result;government.poll | government.poll_opposition | CH-poll | reporter | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about the election that has just taken place: who won, and what the result means for government spending.
G-boost | Politics | politics | government.boost_window | government.purchases_change;government.next_election | government.poll | CH-purchases | critic;business;economist | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about the government spending more in the run-up to the coming election.
G-spending | Politics | purchases | abs(government.purchases_change) >= threshold('g_spending') | government.purchases | | CH-purchases | reporter;business;economist | TRUE | FALSE | FALSE | Write about a clear change in government spending: how much the government buys compared with its normal level, and how that changed.
G-poll | Politics | politics | TRUE | government.poll | government.purchases;government.poll_opposition | CH-poll | reporter | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | Write a short report on the poll: how much support the party in office has.
G-budget | Politics | purchases | TRUE | government.purchases | | CH-purchases | reporter | FALSE | TRUE | FALSE | Write a short report on government spending compared with its normal level.
A-analysis | Analysis | no politics | TRUE | pressing.variable;drivers.output;drivers.inflation | public.expected_inflation | | economist;critic | FALSE | FALSE | FALSE | Write an analysis of {figure}: where it stands against its normal, and what moved it most last quarter.
")

# Section 4.2.2: the analysis's assignment in a quarter where no figure stands far from its normal
analysis_quiet <- "Write an analysis of a quiet quarter: why inflation, growth and unemployment all stand close to their normal levels."

# Section 4.2.2: the fields a piece carries only where the topic has the bank's word
word_fields <- c("public.trust_percent", "word.path", "word.room")
